From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:35:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(core): pin prctl admission option and argument bounds

### What
Pins `balanced_arguments_allowed` for syscall 302 (prctl): admission requires `arg0 == 0` and `arg1 <= 15`; the test covers the exact boundary (15 admitted, 16 rejected) and a nonzero option.

### Why it matters
The prctl arm had no direct test. Widening the argument bound or dropping the option check would silently over-admit while passing the existing suite.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| drop `arg0 == 0` check | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| `arg1 <= 15` -> `arg1 <= 16` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-core --lib prctl_admission`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
index 579e56e2..50048b6a 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
@@ -959,4 +959,14 @@ mod tests {
         assert_eq!(balanced_surface(9), BalancedSurface::Memory);
         assert_eq!(balanced_surface(999), BalancedSurface::Denied);
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn prctl_admission_pins_option_and_arg_bounds() {
+        // option must be 0, arg1 <= 15
+        assert!(balanced_arguments_allowed(302, 0, 0, 0));
+        assert!(balanced_arguments_allowed(302, 0, 15, 0));
+        assert!(!balanced_arguments_allowed(302, 0, 16, 0));
+        assert!(!balanced_arguments_allowed(302, 1, 0, 0));
+        assert!(!balanced_arguments_allowed(302, 0, 100, 0));
+    }
 }
